  "item": [
    {
      "id": "f7038a2f-b2e6-4a53-9260-474277022890",
      "name": "records",
      "description": {
        "content": "Call Records Management",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "b537b2c9-641e-483f-a7dc-8809cac6eb14",
          "name": "Get, stream, and search call records",
          "request": {
            "name": "Get, stream, and search call records",
            "description": {
              "content": "Get the latest call records. They can be filtered by number, name, time or type.\n\nThe response format is controlled by the `Accept` request header:\n\n`application/json` *(default)*:\n\nReturns a JSON array of call records.\n\n`text/event-stream`:\n\nStreams call records as Server-Sent Events (SSE).\n\nEach event carries one JSON-encoded call record in its `data` field.\nA record will be **re-sent** if it is updated after initial delivery. The most common update case is transcription processing: a call with transcription activated is first streamed with `transcription.available: false` (audio processing still in progress). Once processing completes, the **same record** — identified by the same `uuid` — is streamed again with `transcription.available: true` and an `updated` timestamp. Clients should use `uuid` to detect such updates and replace the previously received record accordingly.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "records"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "search",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "Search the records. The search looks at the caller and callee names and numbers. Any other call record fields are currently not considered when searching"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "filter",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "Filter call records that match certain property values.\n\nIt is possible to specify multiple filters by providing a comma separated list. In this case only records that match all filters will be returned in the result.\n\nFor compatibility reasons, the `customer` and `extension` filters are treated as separate query parameters."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "customer",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "The K-number for which to return call records. Applies only to admin level access with appropriate permissions"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "extension",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "The extension (user) for which to return call records. Applies to admin level access with appropriate permissions"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "from",
                  "value": "<number>",
                  "description": "Limit the list to records that are newer than this timestamp."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "to",
                  "value": "<number>",
                  "description": "Limit the list to records that are older than this timestamp"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "0",
                  "description": "Limit the number of call records in the result."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "offset",
                  "value": "0",
                  "description": "Generate the list starting from offset"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "complete",
                  "value": "false",
                  "description": "Should the records include the complete transcripts and summaries (for transcribed calls)."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "sort",
                  "value": "desc",
                  "description": "Set creation time sort order"
                }
              ],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{bearerToken}}"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "id": "218b4473-f999-440e-af06-a9b3b00e2e1f",
              "name": "Call records. The response format depends on the `Accept` request header:\n- `application/json` (default): a JSON array of call records.\n- `text/event-stream`: a Server-Sent Events (SSE) stream of call records. Records are delivered in chronological order.",
